description:
A Call-Off (Concession) Contract for the provision of Enforcement Agents Services. The Council conducted a further competition using the Crown Commercial Service (CCS) Debt Resolution Services Framework (RM6226) Lot 5 &quot;Enforcement Services&quot;. The service provision will collect Debt on behalf of the Council, seek to collect payments in full, or establish payment arrangements in line with the Council&#039;s instructions. The service will also ensure secure, accurate and timely pay-over of Debt collected to the Council. 

The following services will be commissioned under the Call-Off Contracts in relation to Council Tax, Business Rates, Business Improvement Districts (BIDS) and Parking Enforcement:

•	Enforcement action including;
•	Visits;
•	Immobilising Vehicles and Taking Control of Goods;
•	Sale of Goods;
•	Information Sharing and Targeted Enforcement.

Additionally, collection of Housing Benefit Overpayment and Sundry Debts is sought under the Call-Off Contract. The Service will treat customers fairly in accordance with the Public Sector Equality Duty and in compliance with Harrow policies.
